<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Lincoln is a 32-year-old man with major depressive disorder, single episode, in early remission on sertraline 50 mg daily (PHQ-9 4 nine days ago), who asked for a same-day visit. Three days ago he spent an afternoon in shorts and a short-sleeved shirt clearing overgrown brush and vines at a friend&apos;s property. The next morning itchy red streaks appeared on both forearms, then blisters, spreading over two days to the backs of both hands, the right side of his neck, and both shins. The itch woke him repeatedly on the last two nights, and he worries that the poor sleep means his depression is coming back. He says his mood itself is unchanged and he has had no suicidal thoughts. Calamine lotion and cool showers help briefly. He has not yet washed the clothes or gloves he wore. He has no fever, eye swelling, genital involvement, or trouble breathing, and he has never had a stomach ulcer. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>The morning after clearing brush and vines three days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Both forearms, backs of both hands, right side of the neck, and both shins</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days, still spreading</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Itchy red streaks and blisters, some weeping</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Severe itch; sleep broken on two nights</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Itch worst at night</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Outdoor brush clearing with bare arms and legs</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Calamine and cool showers help briefly</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Poor sleep from itch. Denies fever, eye or facial swelling, genital rash, wheeze, low mood, and suicidal thoughts</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

